{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-mic-6-1","title":"Micah 6:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God's controversy for ingratitude; 6 for ignorance, 10 for injustice; 16 and for idolatry.</p>\n<p>ye. 1:2; 1Sa 15:16; Jer 13:15; Am 3:1; Heb 3:7,8 Arise.The manner of raising attention, says Abp. Newcome, in ver. 1, 2, by calling a man to urge his plea in the face of all nature, and on the inanimate creation to hear the expostulation of Jehovah with his people, is truly awakening and magnificent. The words of Jehovah follow in ver. 3-5; and God's mercies having been set before the people, one of them is introduced in a beautiful manner, asking what his duty is towards so gracious a God, ver. 6, 7. The answer follows in the words of the prophet, ver. 8.</p>\n<p>contend. De 4:26; 32:1; Ps 50:1,4; Isa 1:2; Jer 22:29; Eze 36:1,8; Lu 19:40 before. or, with. 1:4; Isa 2:12-14 let. Eze 37:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-2","title":"Micah 6:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>foundations. De 32:22; 2Sa 22:8,16; Ps 104:5; Pr 8:29; Jer 31:37 a controversy. Isa 1:18; 5:3; 43:26; Jer 2:9,29-35; 25:31; Eze 20:35,36; Ho 4:1 Ho 12:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-3","title":"Micah 6:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>O my. 5; Ps 50:7; 81:8,13 what. Jer 2:5,31 wherein. Isa 43:22,23 testify. Ps 51:4; Ro 3:4,5,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-4","title":"Micah 6:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>I brought. Ex 12:51; 14:30,31; 20:2; De 4:20,34; 5:6; 9:26; Ne 9:9-11 Ps 78:51-53; 106:7-10; 136:10,11; Isa 63:9-12; Jer 32:21 Eze 20:5-9; Am 2:10; Ac 7:36 and redeemed. De 7:8; 15:15; 24:18; 2Sa 7:23 Moses. Ex 15:20,21; Nu 12:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-5","title":"Micah 6:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>remember. De 8:2,18; 9:7; 16:3; Ps 103:1,2; 111:4; Eph 2:11 Balak. Nu 22:1-25:18; 31:16; De 23:4,5; Jos 24:9,10; Re 2:14 Balaam. Nu 31:8; 2Pe 2:15; Jude 1:11 Shittim. Nu 22:41; 23:13,14,27; 25:1; 33:49; Jos 4:19; 5:9,10; 10:42,43 know. Jud 5:11; *marg: Ps 36:10; 71:15,16,19; 143:11; Ro 3:25,26; 1Jo 1:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-6","title":"Micah 6:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Wherewith. 2Sa 21:3; Mt 19:16; Lu 10:25; Joh 6:26; Ac 2:37; 16:30; Ro 10:2,3 bow. Ps 22:29; 95:6; Eph 3:14 the high. Ge 14:18-22; Da 3:26; 4:9; 5:18,21; Mr 5:7; Ac 16:17 with. Le 1:3-17; Nu 23:1-4,14,15,29,30; Heb 10:4-10 of a year old. Heb. sons of a year. Ex 12:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-7","title":"Micah 6:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>pleased. 1Sa 15:22; Ps 10:8-13; 50:9; 51:16; Isa 1:11-15; 40:16; Jer 7:21,22 Ho 6:6; Am 5:22 rivers. Job 29:6 shall. Jud 11:31,39; 2Ki 3:27; 16:3; 21:6; 23:10; Jer 7:31; 19:5 Eze 16:20,21; 23:37 body. Heb. belly. Phm 1:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-8","title":"Micah 6:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>O man. Ro 9:20; 1Co 7:16; Jas 2:20 what is. 1Sa 12:23; Ne 9:13; Ps 73:28; La 3:26; Lu 10:42; Ro 7:16; 2Th 2:16 and what. De 10:12,13 to do. Ge 18:19; 1Sa 15:22; Pr 21:3; Ec 12:13; Isa 1:16-19; 58:6-11 Jer 7:3-6; Ho 6:6; 12:6; Am 5:24; Zep 2:3; Mt 3:8-10; Mr 12:30-34 Lu 11:42; Tit 2:11,12; 2Pe 1:5-8 love. Ps 37:26; 112:4,9; Isa 57:1,2; Mt 5:7; 18:32-35; Lu 6:36; Eph 4:32 Col 3:12; 1Pe 3:8 walk humbly. Heb. humble thyself to walk. Ge 5:22; Le 26:41; 2Ch 30:11; 32:26; 33:12,13,19,23; 34:27 Isa 57:15; 66:2; Eze 16:63; Da 4:37; Mt 5:3; Lu 18:13-17; Ro 10:1-3 Jas 4:6-10; 1Pe 5:5,6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-9","title":"Micah 6:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Lord's. 3:12; Isa 24:10-12; 27:10; 32:13,14; 40:6-8; 66:6; Jer 19:11-13 Jer 26:6,18; 37:8-10; Ho 13:16; Am 2:5; 3:8-15; 6:1; Jon 3:4; Zep 3:2 and. 2Ki 22:11-20; Ps 107:43; Pr 22:3; Isa 26:11; Ho 14:9 the man of wisdom shall see thy name. or, thy name shall seethat which is wisdom. Ex 34:5-7; Ps 9:16; 48:10; 83:18; Isa 30:27 hear. 2Sa 21:1; Job 5:6-8,17; 10:2; Isa 9:13; 10:5,6; Jer 14:18-22 La 3:39-42; Joe 2:11-18; Am 4:6-12; Jon 3:5-10; Hag 1:5-7; Re 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-10","title":"Micah 6:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Are, etc. or, Is there yet unto every man an house of thewicked, etc. the treasures. Jos 7:1; 2Ki 5:23,24; Pr 10:2; 21:6; Jer 5:26,27; Am 3:10 Hab 2:5-11; Zep 1:9; Zec 5:3,4; Jas 5:1-4 and. Le 19:35,36; De 25:13-16; Pr 11:1; 20:10,23; Eze 45:9-12; Ho 12:7,8 Am 8:5,6 scant measure. Heb. measure of leanness.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-11","title":"Micah 6:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>count them pure. or, be pure. the wicked. Ho 12:7 the bag. Pr 16:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-12","title":"Micah 6:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>the rich. 2:1,2; 3:1-3,9-11; 7:2-6; Isa 1:23; 5:7; Jer 5:5,6,26-29; 6:6,7 Eze 22:6-13,25-29; Ho 4:1,2; Am 5:11,12; 6:1-3; Zep 3:3 spoken. Isa 59:3-15; Jer 9:2-6,8; Ho 7:1,13; Ro 3:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-13","title":"Micah 6:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>I make. Le 26:16; De 28:21,22; Job 33:19-22; Ps 107:17,18; Isa 1:5,6 Jer 14:18; Ac 12:23 in. La 1:13; 3:11; Ho 5:9; 13:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-14","title":"Micah 6:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>eat. Le 26:26; Isa 65:13; Eze 4:16,17; Ho 4:10; Hag 1:6; 2:16 and thou. De 32:22-25; Isa 3:6-8; 24:17-20; Jer 48:44; Eze 5:12; Am 2:14-16 Am 9:1-4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-15","title":"Micah 6:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>Le 26:20; De 28:38-40; Isa 62:8,9; 65:21,22; Jer 12:13; Joe 1:10-12 Am 5:11; Zep 1:13; Hag 1:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-mic-6-16","title":"Micah 6:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"MIC","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>the statutes of Omri are kept. or, he doth much keep the,etc. 1Ki 16:25-30; Ho 5:11 the works. 1Ki 16:30-33; 18:4; 21:25,26; 2Ki 16:3; 21:3; Isa 9:16; Re 2:20 ye walk. Ps 1:1; Jer 7:24 that. 1Ki 9:8; 2Ch 29:8,9; 34:25; Jer 18:15,16; 19:8; 21:8,9; Eze 8:17,18 desolation. or, astonishment. therefore. Ps 44:13; Isa 25:8; Jer 51:51; La 5:1; Eze 39:26; Da 9:16</p>"}]}